  "content_text": "For the past couple of weeks, you could get my latest book — The Secret Life of Circuits — directly from the publisher. That said, I know that some of you don’t want Jeff Bezos to starve, so I’m happy to announce that it’s now in stock on Amazon: Buy on Amazon Prospective readers in Europe can place orders on amazon.de , amazon.fr , amazon.pl , amazon.es , amazon.nl , amazon.se , amazon.it , and amazon.co.uk . The book is also available from Barnes & Noble and other major online retailers in the US and Canada. We conducted rigorous tests to confirm the book is free of AI slop. While I have you here, a small plea: if you read The Secret Life of Circuits and have an Amazon account, please consider leaving an honest review. Reviews matter for their recommendation algorithm, and in 2026, every human author is “competing” with hundreds of AI-generated books . There’s even AI title-squatting going on: Of course, both Jeff and I thank you for your patronage!",
